// SEVERAL RESULTS — the negative product. Consumed in the same reduction it
// expect: 1 4 7 10 16 25 40 64 103
// vanishes entirely; what reaches a backend is only the case that crosses a
// boundary, and each host spells that its own way: Go's multiple return, a Java
// record, a JavaScript object, rax/rdx on x86 (values.md §4).
//
// Here it is consumed in place, so the right answer is that nothing is built.
fn divmod2(n) { (n + 1, n * 2) }

fn run(n) {
    (a, b) = divmod2(n)
    a + b
}
